# The edition is a single file that gets archived under a DOI and cited by hash, so its
# bytes must not depend on the machine that checked it out. Git's autocrlf would give a
# Windows working copy CRLF and a Linux one LF — same commit, two different documents.
# Normalise everything to LF in the repository and on checkout; the build writes LF too
# (every output opens with newline='\n').
* text=auto eol=lf
